<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="34488" href="schedule/2011/spring/SOC/596/34488.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2011" href="schedule/2011.xml">2011</calendarYear><term id="120111" href="schedule/2011/spring.xml">Spring 2011</term><subject id="SOC" href="schedule/2011/spring/SOC.xml">Sociology</subject><course id="596" href="schedule/2011/spring/SOC/596.xml">Recent Developments in Soc</course></parents><sectionNumber>AZ </sectionNumber><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Topic:  Family Diversity and Change in the 21st Century.  Focus on faculty and student authored papers on diverse families, and interdisciplinary collaboration to reconstitute family norms for the 21st century and explore its implications.  This project will be approached from an intersectional perspective that considers the impact of race, class, gender, sexuality, ability and other social categories on modern family formations globally.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Not intended for Undergrad - Urbana-Champaign. </sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2011-01-18Z</startDate><endDate>2011-05-04Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="S2 ">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>09:30 AM</start><end>11:50 AM</end><daysOfTheWeek>F      </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>166</roomNumber><buildingName>Wohlers Hall</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Zerai" firstName="A">Zerai, A</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>